// Q-163 Nothing limits how long a request computes: a loop that never ends holds its instance until the process is killed, with no log line. Expected: `--max-compute`, ending it as a 500 at a statement boundary
// mode: script
// script: steps.sh
// open-when: no such limit
// open-when: answer with a limit: 000
// fixed-when: answer with a limit: 500
// From FEEDBACK20.md §Q-163 (found on 9e8c2fb). The plan is watchdog, deadline, check warning, never preemption.

route GET /forever {
    let i = 0
    while true { i = i + 1 }
    "never"
}
